# Webcam (vis) lens calibration, read by compare_replay.py (toggle: v).
#
# Blank lines and anything after # are ignored. fx = 0 means "not filled in
# yet" and the undistort toggle stays disabled for this camera.
#
#   model          pinhole  - OpenCV cv2.calibrateCamera model
#                  fisheye  - cv2.fisheye model (dist is then k1 k2 k3 k4)
#   width height   resolution the calibration was done at. K is rescaled
#                  if the recording differs; distortion is scale-free
#   fx fy cx cy    camera matrix K = [[fx 0 cx] [0 fy cy] [0 0 1]], pixels
#   dist           pinhole: k1 k2 p1 p2 [k3 [k4 k5 k6 [s1 s2 s3 s4 [tx ty]]]]
#                  fisheye: k1 k2 k3 k4
model   pinhole
# From MATLAB cameraIntrinsics (ImageSize [1080 1920] = rows cols).
# cx/cy shifted by -1: MATLAB pixel coords are 1-based, OpenCV's are 0-based.
width   1920
height  1080
fx      1006.6
fy      999.7485
cx      988.8375
cy      505.3169
dist    -0.2754 0.0560 0 0
